# Global config shared across all apps in this repo (not to be
# confused with each app's own apps/<id>/.env). Copied to .env
# automatically the first time you run `make bootstrap`, `make
# set-storage`, or any app's install.sh.

# Directory used as the *default* base for every app's data, so you can
# point one external drive (or any other path) at all of them at once
# instead of setting DATA_DIR by hand in every app's own .env. Blank =
# each app keeps using its own ./data folder (unchanged behavior).
#
# When set, e.g.:
#   GLOBAL_STORAGE_DIR=/mnt/external/catasophie
# each app's installer defaults its DATA_DIR to
# "<GLOBAL_STORAGE_DIR>/<app-id>" - e.g. wikimed defaults to
# /mnt/external/catasophie/wikimed, offline-maps to
# /mnt/external/catasophie/offline-maps, etc. Still fully overridable
# per app (its own install.sh prompt, or editing apps/<id>/.env
# directly). Changing this later only affects apps not yet installed
# (or reinstalled after clearing their own DATA_DIR) - it does not move
# any already-installed app's existing data. Use `make set-storage` to
# view/change this later.
GLOBAL_STORAGE_DIR=
